The ESA requires employers with 25+ employees (counted each January 1) to maintain written policies on both disconnecting from work and electronic monitoring. When a policy is prepared or revised, a copy must be given to every employee within 30 days (new hires also receive it within 30 days of hire).  

- A, D and E all have fewer than 25 employees on 1 Jan 2023, so neither policy is required; they are compliant.  
- B has only 23 employees, so no policy is required; voluntary non-distribution creates no violation.  
- C has ~1 000 employees and therefore must follow the 30-day distribution rule. Updating monthly yet distributing only quarterly necessarily exceeds the 30-day window for at least some revisions, placing C out of compliance on 2 Jan 2023.}

