The ESA requires Ontario employers with 25+ employees (counted on January 1 of the given year) to maintain both a written disconnecting-from-work policy and a written electronic-monitoring policy. A copy of each policy (or any revision) must be given to every employee within 30 days and to every new hire within 30 days of hire.

- A, B, D and E all have fewer than 25 employees on 1 Jan 2023, so neither policy is mandatory; any omissions or partial distribution are therefore lawful.
- C has ~1 000 employees on 1 Jan 2023 and therefore must satisfy the 30-day distribution rule. Updating monthly yet distributing only quarterly necessarily exceeds the 30-day window for at least some revisions, violating the ESA. Hence C is the only non-compliant employer as of 2 Jan 2023.}

